## TESTING PROTOCOL (MANDATORY — DO NOT SKIP)

### Pre-Implementation Snapshot

```bash
# Export current config as baseline
ddev drush config-export --destination=/path/to/config-backup-pre-commerce
git add -A && git commit -m "chore: pre-commerce config snapshot"
```

### Testing Gates — Stop at Each Gate

**Gate 1 — Module Installation**
- [ ] `drush status` shows all new modules enabled with no errors
- [ ] Existing pages load without PHP errors or white screens
- [ ] Canvas editor still opens and saves content
- [ ] Theme CSS/JS assets load (check browser DevTools Network tab)

**Gate 2 — Commerce Configuration**
- [ ] A test product (membership plan) can be created and saved
- [ ] The checkout flow renders correctly on desktop and mobile
- [ ] No JS console errors on checkout pages
- [ ] Pricing cards SDC renders with correct `--hg-` token values

**Gate 3 — Payment Gateway (Stripe Sandbox)**
- [ ] Stripe test mode keys are loaded from `.env` — verify with `ddev drush config:get commerce_stripe.stripe_checkout_settings` and confirm keys start with `pk_test_` / `sk_test_`
- [ ] Complete a test purchase using Stripe's test card `4242 4242 4242 4242` (any future expiry, any CVC)
- [ ] Test a declined card using `4000 0000 0000 0002` — confirm checkout handles the error gracefully without a white screen or data loss
- [ ] Confirm the `premium_member` role (or tier-specific role) is granted to the test user after successful purchase — check via `ddev drush user:information [username]`
- [ ] Confirm a Stripe subscription object was created in the Stripe Dashboard (test mode)
- [ ] Confirm gated content becomes visible to the test user
- [ ] Confirm gated content remains hidden to an anonymous user and a logged-in non-member

**Gate 4 — Subscription Lifecycle**
- [ ] Simulate subscription renewal (advance cron date in dev)
- [ ] Simulate subscription cancellation and confirm role revocation
- [ ] Simulate failed payment and confirm grace period behavior (as defined in Clarification Phase)

**Gate 5 — Regression**
- [ ] All pre-existing public pages still load without errors
- [ ] Canvas editor works on non-gated content types
- [ ] Theme design tokens unchanged (run visual diff if possible)
- [ ] Accessibility audit — paywall components pass keyboard navigation and screen reader tests

### Rollback Plan

If any gate fails:
```bash
# Revert to pre-commerce config snapshot
ddev drush config-import --source=/path/to/config-backup-pre-commerce
ddev drush cr
# Uninstall new modules cleanly
ddev drush pm-uninstall commerce_license commerce_recurring commerce -y
```

