## SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

- Payment credentials loaded via environment variables only (never in `settings.php` literals)
- **Before writing any Stripe keys**, confirm `.env` exists and is listed in `.gitignore`:
  ```bash
  # Confirm .env is gitignored
  grep -n ".env" .gitignore
  # If not present, add it immediately before proceeding
  echo ".env" >> .gitignore
  git add .gitignore && git commit -m "chore: ensure .env is gitignored before adding secrets"
  ```
- Stripe keys must be set in `.env` using this naming convention:
  ```dotenv
  STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
  STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
  ```
  And read in `settings.php` via:
  ```php
  $config['commerce_stripe.stripe_checkout_settings']['secret_key'] = getenv('STRIPE_SECRET_KEY');
  $config['commerce_stripe.stripe_checkout_settings']['publishable_key'] = getenv('STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY');
  ```
- Switch from `pk_test_` / `sk_test_` to live keys only when the developer gives explicit written approval in this chat
- PCI compliance delegated entirely to Stripe (no raw card data touches Drupal — Stripe.js handles tokenization client-side)
- Role grant/revoke logic handled server-side by `commerce_license` — never client-side
- All new admin pages restricted to `administrator` role minimum
- CSRF tokens on all custom form submissions

